sections.content:
A basic functional component:
function Header() {
  return <header><h1>My Site</h1></header>;
}

Composing components by nesting them like custom HTML tags:
function App() {
  return (
    <div>
      <Header />
      <MainContent />
      <Footer />
    </div>
  );
}

A component file is typically exported so other files can import and use it:
export default function Header() {
  return <header><h1>My Site</h1></header>;
}
// in another file:
import Header from './Header';

This import/export pattern (ES modules, briefly touched on in earlier modules) is how a real React project splits components across multiple files rather than cramming everything into one enormous file.

